cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "UbboTELORNA"
abstract: >
  UbboTELORNA annotates three classes of ancient, conserved genomic elements —
  telomeres, rRNA genes, and tRNA genes — in genome assemblies, with built-in
  low-complexity masking to prevent failures on telomeric and repetitive sequences.
  Named after Ubbo-Sathla, the primordial source of all terrestrial life in the
  Lovecraft–Smith Mythos.
